    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0944" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/7–1345</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-13">July 13, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The attached memorandum entitled “U. S. Interpretation of the Yalta Agreement and
                    Terms Which China Might Appropriately Accept <pb facs="0945" n="935"
                        xml:id="pg935"/> in Regard to Outer Mongolia and, Manchuria”, has been
                    prepared in pursuance to the suggestion contained in Ambassador Harriman’s
                    081800 and your request sent through Admiral Leahy (MR–IN–19).<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d662-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>There is in the Department no copy of the Yalta Agreement or of any records of
                    conversations relating thereto. The attached memorandum has therefore been
                    prepared on the basis of our recollection of its contents.</p>
                <p>You may wish to give special attention to the portions of the memorandum which
                    have been marked in red.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d662-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d662-a1.xml" xpointer="d662-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d662-f1" n="89" xml:id="d662-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Secretary of State requested Mr. Grew to prepare the studies
                    recommended by Ambassador Harriman in his telegrams 081750 and 081800 of July
                    8.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d662-f2" n="90" xml:id="d662-f2-content">
                <p>File copy does not indicate portions marked in red.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
